1
00:00:03,119 --> 00:00:04,220
Chapter 16.

2
00:00:06,369 --> 00:00:09,325
I both wished and feared to see Mr. Rochester

3
00:00:09,326 --> 00:00:12,419
on the day which followed this sleepless night.

4
00:00:13,509 --> 00:00:17,540
I wanted to hear his voice again, yet feared to meet his eye.

5
00:00:19,044 --> 00:00:22,860
During the early part of the morning, I momentarily expected his coming.

6
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:26,919
He was not in the frequent habit of entering the school room.

7
00:00:27,750 --> 00:00:30,299
But he did step in for a few minutes sometimes.

8
00:00:31,299 --> 00:00:34,560
And I had the impression that he was sure to visit it that day.

9
00:00:35,659 --> 00:00:38,240
But the morning passed just as usual.

10
00:00:39,159 --> 00:00:42,919
Nothing happened to interrupt the quiet course of Adele's studies.

11
00:00:44,509 --> 00:00:49,279
Only soon after breakfast, I heard some bustle in the neighborhood of Mr.

12
00:00:49,439 --> 00:00:52,149
Rochester's chamber, Mrs. Fairfax's voice

13
00:00:52,150 --> 00:00:56,241
and liars and the cooks, that is John's wife.

14
00:00:56,560 --> 00:01:00,770
And even John's own gruff tones, there were exclamations

15
00:01:00,771 --> 00:01:03,580
of what a mercy master was not burned in his bed.

16
00:01:04,759 --> 00:01:07,200
It is always dangerous to keep a candle lit at night.

17
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:12,540
How providential that he had presence of mind to think of the water jug.

18
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:15,540
I wonder he waked nobody.

19
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:22,020
It is to be hoped he will not take cold with sleeping on the library sofa, etc.

20
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:28,299
To much confabulation succeeded a sound of scrubbing and setting to rights.

21
00:01:29,479 --> 00:01:34,500
And when I passed the room in going downstairs to dinner, I saw through the

22
00:01:34,501 --> 00:01:38,520
open door that awe was again restored to complete order.

23
00:01:39,479 --> 00:01:42,340
Only the bed was stripped of its hangings.

24
00:01:43,319 --> 00:01:49,361
Lea stood up in the window seat, rubbing the pains of glass dimmed with smoke.

25
00:01:49,810 --> 00:01:51,765
I was about to address her, for I wished to

26
00:01:51,766 --> 00:01:55,041
know what account had been given of the affair.

27
00:01:55,759 --> 00:02:01,200
But on advancing, I saw a second person in the chamber, a woman sitting on a chair by

28
00:02:01,201 --> 00:02:04,180
the bedside and sowing rings to new curtains.

29
00:02:05,330 --> 00:02:08,700
That woman was no other than grace pool.

30
00:02:10,159 --> 00:02:15,340
There she sat, stayed and taciturn looking, as usual, in her brown stuffed

31
00:02:15,341 --> 00:02:18,720
gown, her check apron, white and couchiff and cap.

32
00:02:19,689 --> 00:02:23,700
She was intent on her work, in which her whole thoughts seemed absorbed.

33
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:30,000
On her hard forehead, and in her commonplace features, was nothing either

34
00:02:30,001 --> 00:02:34,939
of the paleness or desperation, one would have expected to see marking the

35
00:02:34,940 --> 00:02:39,179
countenance of a woman who had attempted murder, and whose

36
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:42,720
intended victim had followed her last night to her lair.

37
00:02:43,279 --> 00:02:48,040
And, as I believed, charged her with the crime she wished to perpetrate.

38
00:02:49,165 --> 00:02:55,959
I was amazed, confounded, she looked up, while I still gazed at her, no start,

39
00:02:56,580 --> 00:03:01,240
no increase or failure of color, betrayed emotion, consciousness of guilt

40
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:03,000
or fear of detection.

41
00:03:09,580 --> 00:03:17,580
She said, good morning, miss, in her usual I will put her to some test, thought I.

42
00:03:18,700 --> 00:03:22,740
Such absolute impenetrability is past comprehension.

43
00:03:24,099 --> 00:03:26,340
Good morning, grace, I said.

44
00:03:27,220 --> 00:03:28,419
Has anything happened here?

45
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:32,180
I thought I heard the servants all talking together a while ago.

46
00:03:33,340 --> 00:03:36,459
Only master had been reading in his bed last night.

47
00:03:37,549 --> 00:03:41,340
He fell asleep with his candle lit, and the curtains got on fire.

48
00:03:42,250 --> 00:03:48,599
But, fortunately, he awoke before the bedclothes or the woodwork caught and

49
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:52,299
contrived to quench the flames with the water in the ure.

50
00:03:53,509 --> 00:03:59,900
A strange affair, I said, in a low voice, then looking at her fixedly, did Mr.

51
00:04:00,119 --> 00:04:01,400
Rochester wake nobody?

52
00:04:02,340 --> 00:04:03,819
Did no one hear him move?

53
00:04:05,330 --> 00:04:08,657
She again raised her eyes to me, and this time there

54
00:04:08,658 --> 00:04:11,520
was something of consciousness in their expression.

55
00:04:12,740 --> 00:04:16,439
She seemed to examine me wearily, then she answered.

56
00:04:17,650 --> 00:04:20,200
The servants sleep so far off, you know, miss.

57
00:04:21,189 --> 00:04:22,840
They would not be likely to hear.

58
00:04:23,779 --> 00:04:28,978
Mrs. Fairfax room, and yours are the nearest to masters, but Mrs.

59
00:04:28,979 --> 00:04:31,099
Fairfax said she heard nothing.

60
00:04:32,569 --> 00:04:38,700
When people get elderly, they often sleep heavy, she paused, and then added with a

61
00:04:38,701 --> 00:04:43,619
sort of assumed indifference, but still in a marked and significant tone.

62
00:04:44,919 --> 00:04:48,680
But you are young, miss, and I should say a light sleeper.

63
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:51,279
Perhaps you may have heard a noise.

64
00:04:52,694 --> 00:04:58,240
I did, said I, dropping my voice, so that Leah, who was still polishing the

65
00:04:58,241 --> 00:05:01,959
pains, could not hear me, and at first I thought it was pilot.

66
00:05:03,034 --> 00:05:04,419
But pilot cannot laugh.

67
00:05:05,569 --> 00:05:08,860
And I am certain I heard a laugh and a strange one.

68
00:05:10,250 --> 00:05:15,479
She took a new needle full of thread, waxed it carefully, threaded her needle

69
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:20,680
with a steady hand, and then observed with perfect composure.

70
00:05:21,479 --> 00:05:23,360
It is hardly likely master would laugh.

71
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:26,779
I should think, miss, when he was in such danger.

72
00:05:27,580 --> 00:05:28,900
You must have been dreaming.

73
00:05:30,380 --> 00:05:37,620
I was not dreaming, I said, with some warmth, for her brazen coolness provoked me.

74
00:05:38,009 --> 00:05:42,779
Again, she looked at me, and with the same scrutinizing and conscious eye.

75
00:05:43,599 --> 00:05:45,900
Have you told master that you heard a laugh?

76
00:05:46,779 --> 00:05:47,779
She inquired.

77
00:05:48,569 --> 00:05:51,360
I have not had the opportunity of speaking to him this morning.

78
00:05:52,659 --> 00:05:55,979
You did not think of opening your door and looking out into the gallery?

79
00:05:56,819 --> 00:05:57,819
She further asked.

80
00:05:58,669 --> 00:06:00,554
She appeared to be cross questioning me,

81
00:06:00,555 --> 00:06:03,760
attempting to draw from me information unawares.

82
00:06:04,590 --> 00:06:10,299
The idea struck me, that if she discovered I knew or suspected her guilt,

83
00:06:11,069 --> 00:06:14,099
she would be playing of some of her malignant pranks on me.

84
00:06:14,979 --> 00:06:17,119
I thought it advisable to be on my guard.

85
00:06:18,860 --> 00:06:23,400
On the contrary, said I, I bolted my door.

86
00:06:24,979 --> 00:06:26,958
Then you are not in the habit of bolting your

87
00:06:26,959 --> 00:06:30,120
door every night before you get into bed.

88
00:06:31,220 --> 00:06:36,979
Fiend, she wants to know my habits that she may lay her plans accordingly.

89
00:06:38,340 --> 00:06:40,740
Indignation again prevailed over prudence.

90
00:06:41,439 --> 00:06:42,439
I replied sharply.

91
00:06:43,479 --> 00:06:46,419
Hither too, I have often omitted to fasten the bolt.

92
00:06:47,290 --> 00:06:48,680
I did not think it necessary.

93
00:06:49,439 --> 00:06:53,759
I was not aware any danger or annoyance was to be dreaded at Thornfield Hall.

94
00:06:54,950 --> 00:07:00,168
But in future, and I laid marked stress on the words, I shall

95
00:07:00,169 --> 00:07:04,220
take good care to make all secure before I venture to lie down.

96
00:07:06,090 --> 00:07:08,860
It will be wise so to do was her answer.

97
00:07:09,959 --> 00:07:14,548
This neighborhood is as quiet as any I know, and I never heard

98
00:07:14,549 --> 00:07:18,580
of the hall being attempted by robbers since it was a house.

99
00:07:19,779 --> 00:07:22,315
Though there are hundreds of pounds worth of

100
00:07:22,316 --> 00:07:25,901
plate in the plate closet, as is well known.

101
00:07:26,479 --> 00:07:30,864
And you see, for such a large house, there are very

102
00:07:30,865 --> 00:07:34,119
few servants, because master has never lived here much.

103
00:07:34,900 --> 00:07:39,419
And when he does come, being a bachelor, he needs little waiting on.

104
00:07:40,450 --> 00:07:43,220
But I always think it best to err on the safe side.

105
00:07:44,080 --> 00:07:47,783
A door is soon fastened, and it is as well to have a

106
00:07:47,784 --> 00:07:51,220
drawn bolt between one and any mischief that may be about.

107
00:07:52,169 --> 00:07:57,840
A deal of people miss are for trusting all to providence, but I say providence will

108
00:07:57,841 --> 00:08:00,683
not dispense with the means, though he often

109
00:08:00,684 --> 00:08:03,841
blesses them when they are used discreetly.

110
00:08:04,759 --> 00:08:08,691
And here she closed her rang, a long one for her,

111
00:08:08,692 --> 00:08:12,180
and uttered with the demureness of a quakerus.

112
00:08:13,224 --> 00:08:19,520
I still stood absolutely dumbfounded at what appeared to me, her miraculous self

113
00:08:19,521 --> 00:08:24,279
-possession, and most inscrutable hypocrisy when the cook entered.

114
00:08:26,060 --> 00:08:28,959
Mrs. Paul said she, addressing grace.

115
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:31,580
The servants dinner will soon be ready.

116
00:08:32,040 --> 00:08:33,040
Will you come down?

117
00:08:33,930 --> 00:08:36,251
No, just put my pint of porter in bit of

118
00:08:36,252 --> 00:08:39,661
pudding on a tray, and I'll carry it upstairs.

119
00:08:40,479 --> 00:08:41,599
You'll have some meat?

120
00:08:42,625 --> 00:08:45,099
Just a morsel and a taste of cheese, that's all.

121
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:47,560
And the sargo?

122
00:08:48,549 --> 00:08:49,759
Never minded at present.

123
00:08:50,924 --> 00:08:52,740
I shall be coming down before tea time.

124
00:08:53,599 --> 00:08:54,599
I'll make it myself.

125
00:08:55,810 --> 00:09:00,159
The cook here turned to me, saying that Mrs. Fairfax was waiting for me,

126
00:09:00,650 --> 00:09:01,650
so I departed.

127
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:07,900
I hardly heard Mrs. Fairfax's account of the curtain conflagration during dinner.

128
00:09:08,740 --> 00:09:14,540
So much was I occupied in puzzling my brains over the enigmatical character of

129
00:09:14,541 --> 00:09:20,779
Grace Paul, and still more in pondering the problem of her position at Thornfield,

130
00:09:21,680 --> 00:09:26,759
and questioning why she had not been given into custody that morning, or,

131
00:09:27,229 --> 00:09:30,799
at the very least, dismissed from her master's service.

132
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:36,139
He had almost as much as declared his conviction of her criminality last night.

133
00:09:37,119 --> 00:09:40,639
What mysterious cause withheld him from accusing her?

134
00:09:41,779 --> 00:09:44,880
Why had he enjoined me to, to secrecy?

135
00:09:45,680 --> 00:09:46,680
It was strange.

136
00:09:47,549 --> 00:09:51,773
A bold, vindictive and haughty gentleman seemed somehow

137
00:09:51,774 --> 00:09:55,240
in the power of one of the meanest of his dependence.

138
00:09:56,799 --> 00:10:02,139
So much in her power that even when she lifted her hand against his life,

139
00:10:02,790 --> 00:10:07,939
he dared not openly charge her with the attempt, much less punish her for it.

140
00:10:09,209 --> 00:10:13,099
Had Grace been young and handsome, I should have been tempted to think that

141
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:18,580
tender of feelings than prudence or fear influenced Mr. Rochester in her behalf.

142
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:25,500
But, hard favored and matronly as she was, the idea could not be admitted.

143
00:10:27,509 --> 00:10:30,939
Yet, I reflected, she has been young once.

144
00:10:31,659 --> 00:10:34,040
Her youth would be contemporary with her masters.

145
00:10:35,189 --> 00:10:38,360
Mrs. Fairfax told me once she had lived here many years.

146
00:10:39,389 --> 00:10:41,200
I don't think she can ever have been pretty.

147
00:10:42,075 --> 00:10:46,979
But, for what I know, she may possess originality and strength of character to

148
00:10:46,980 --> 00:10:49,439
compensate for the want of personal advantages.

149
00:10:50,599 --> 00:10:54,340
Mr. Rochester is an amateur of the decided and eccentric.

150
00:10:55,180 --> 00:10:57,340
Grace is eccentric at least.

151
00:10:58,430 --> 00:11:03,880
What if a former Caprice, a freak very possible to a nature so sudden and

152
00:11:03,881 --> 00:11:09,900
headstrong as his, has delivered him into her power, and she now exercises over his

153
00:11:09,901 --> 00:11:13,256
actions a secret influence, the result of his own

154
00:11:13,257 --> 00:11:17,439
indiscretion, which he cannot shake off and dare not disregard.

155
00:11:18,685 --> 00:11:23,500
But, having reached this point of conjecture, Mrs. Poole's square,

156
00:11:23,799 --> 00:11:30,279
flat figure and uncumly, dry even coarse face, occurred so distinctly to my mind's

157
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:35,520
eye, that I thought, no, impossible, my supposition cannot be correct.

158
00:11:36,590 --> 00:11:41,599
Yet, suggested the secret voice which talks to us in our own hearts,

159
00:11:42,680 --> 00:11:43,979
you are not beautiful either.

160
00:11:44,700 --> 00:11:46,619
And perhaps, Mr. Rochester approves you.

161
00:11:47,279 --> 00:11:49,939
At any rate, you have often felt as if he did.

162
00:11:50,799 --> 00:11:55,580
And last night, remember his words, remember his look, remember his voice.

163
00:11:57,349 --> 00:12:00,675
I well remembered all, language, glance, and

164
00:12:00,676 --> 00:12:03,659
tone seemed at the moment vividly renewed.

165
00:12:04,639 --> 00:12:07,540
I was now in the schoolroom, Adele was drawing.

166
00:12:08,319 --> 00:12:10,479
I bent over her and directed her pencil.

167
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:13,159
She looked up with a sort of start.

168
00:12:26,215 --> 00:12:28,759
I am hot Adele with stooping.

169
00:12:29,759 --> 00:12:30,840
She went on sketching.

170
00:12:31,060 --> 00:12:32,060
I went on thinking.

171
00:12:33,430 --> 00:12:35,700
I hastened to drive from my mind.

172
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:41,619
The hateful notion I had been conceiving, respecting Grace Poole, it disgusted me.

173
00:12:42,279 --> 00:12:45,400
I compared myself with her and found we were different.

174
00:12:46,639 --> 00:12:51,279
Bessie Levin had said I was quite a lady, and she spoke truth.

175
00:12:52,220 --> 00:12:57,080
I was a lady, and now I looked much better than I did when Bessie saw me.

176
00:12:57,869 --> 00:13:02,238
I had more color and more flesh, more life, more vivacity,

177
00:13:02,239 --> 00:13:05,500
because I had brighter hopes and keener enjoyments.

178
00:13:07,340 --> 00:13:11,180
Evening approaches said I, as I looked towards the window.

179
00:13:12,139 --> 00:13:16,222
I have never heard Mr. Rochester's voice or step in the

180
00:13:16,223 --> 00:13:18,901
house today, but surely I shall see him before night.

181
00:13:19,819 --> 00:13:21,259
I feared the meeting in the morning.

182
00:13:22,040 --> 00:13:25,959
Now I desire it, because expectation has been

183
00:13:25,960 --> 00:13:29,840
so long baffled that it is grown impatient.

184
00:13:31,259 --> 00:13:34,380
When dusk actually closed, and when Adele left me to go and

185
00:13:34,381 --> 00:13:39,360
play in the nursery with Sophie, I did most keenly desire it.

186
00:13:39,900 --> 00:13:41,560
I listened for the bell to ring below.

187
00:13:42,430 --> 00:13:44,299
I listened for Lea coming up with a message.

188
00:13:45,040 --> 00:13:48,704
I fancied sometimes I heard Mr. Rochester's own tread, and

189
00:13:48,705 --> 00:13:52,619
I turned to the door, expecting it to open and admit him.

190
00:13:53,990 --> 00:13:55,360
The door remained shut.

191
00:13:56,549 --> 00:13:58,580
Darkness only came in through the window.

192
00:13:59,549 --> 00:14:01,400
Still, it was not late.

193
00:14:02,450 --> 00:14:07,439
He often sent for me at seven and eight o 'clock, and it was yet but six.

194
00:14:08,680 --> 00:14:11,661
Surely I should not be wholly disappointed

195
00:14:11,662 --> 00:14:15,940
tonight, when I had so many things to say to him.

196
00:14:16,290 --> 00:14:18,722
I wanted again to introduce the subject of

197
00:14:18,723 --> 00:14:22,280
Grace Pool, and to hear what he would answer.

198
00:14:22,590 --> 00:14:26,979
I wanted to ask him plainly if he really believed it was she who had made last

199
00:14:26,980 --> 00:14:34,040
night's hideous attempt, and if so, why he kept her wickedness a secret.

200
00:14:35,549 --> 00:14:38,700
It little mattered whether my curiosity irritated him.

201
00:14:39,625 --> 00:14:42,860
I knew the pleasure of vexing and soothing him by turns.

202
00:14:43,639 --> 00:14:46,906
It was one I chiefly delighted in, and a sure

203
00:14:46,907 --> 00:14:50,040
instinct always prevented me from going too far.

204
00:14:50,680 --> 00:14:53,720
Beyond the verge of provocation, I never ventured.

205
00:14:54,310 --> 00:14:58,869
On the extreme brink, I liked well to try my skill, retaining

206
00:14:58,870 --> 00:15:03,040
every minute form of respect, every propriety of my station.

207
00:15:03,759 --> 00:15:07,819
I could still meet him in argument without fear or uneasy restraint.

208
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:11,299
This suited both him and me.

209
00:15:12,509 --> 00:15:14,819
A tread creaked on the stairs at last.

210
00:15:15,840 --> 00:15:20,720
Lea made her appearance, but it was only to intimate that tea was ready in Mrs.

211
00:15:20,979 --> 00:15:21,979
Fairfax's room.

212
00:15:22,369 --> 00:15:27,259
Vither I repaired, glad at least to go downstairs, for that brought me,

213
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:30,680
I imagined, nearer to Mr. Rochester's presence.

214
00:15:32,659 --> 00:15:36,619
You must want your tea, said the good lady, as I joined her.

215
00:15:37,599 --> 00:15:38,860
You ate so little at dinner.

216
00:15:39,869 --> 00:15:41,560
I am afraid, she continued.

217
00:15:42,220 --> 00:15:43,360
You are not well today.

218
00:15:44,159 --> 00:15:45,799
You look flushed and feverish.

219
00:15:46,720 --> 00:15:49,720
Oh, quite well, I never felt better.

220
00:15:50,930 --> 00:15:53,900
Then you must prove it by evinsing a good appetite.

221
00:15:55,049 --> 00:15:57,580
Will you fill the teapot while I knit off this needle?

222
00:15:59,049 --> 00:16:04,200
Having completed her task, she rose to draw down the blind, which she had

223
00:16:04,201 --> 00:16:09,439
hitherto kept up, by way I suppose, of making the most of daylight.

224
00:16:10,310 --> 00:16:14,619
The dusk was now fast-deepening into total obscurity.

225
00:16:16,189 --> 00:16:22,341
It is fair tonight, said she, as she looked through the pains, though not starlight.

226
00:16:22,919 --> 00:16:26,939
Mr. Rochester has, on the whole, had a favourable day for his journey.

227
00:16:28,459 --> 00:16:29,459
Journey?

228
00:16:29,720 --> 00:16:31,200
Is Mr. Rochester gone anywhere?

229
00:16:32,310 --> 00:16:33,740
I did not know he was out.

230
00:16:34,869 --> 00:16:37,540
Oh, he set off the moment he had breakfasted.

231
00:16:38,229 --> 00:16:44,200
He has gone to the knees, Mr. Eston's place, ten miles on the other side, Millcoat.

232
00:16:44,729 --> 00:16:47,040
I believe there is quite a party assembled there.

233
00:16:47,860 --> 00:16:51,919
Lord Ingram, Sir George Lynn, Colonel Dent, and others.

234
00:16:53,744 --> 00:16:55,119
Do you expect him back tonight?

235
00:16:56,400 --> 00:16:57,400
No.

236
00:16:57,689 --> 00:16:59,080
Nor tomorrow, either.

237
00:16:59,939 --> 00:17:02,639
I should think he is very likely to stay a week or more.

238
00:17:03,740 --> 00:17:08,400
When these fine, fashionable people get together, they are so surrounded by

239
00:17:08,401 --> 00:17:13,279
elegance and gayity, so well-provided with all that complies and entertain,

240
00:17:14,139 --> 00:17:16,020
they are in no hurry to separate.

241
00:17:17,299 --> 00:17:23,860
Gentlemen, especially, are often in request on such occasions, and Mr.

242
00:17:24,020 --> 00:17:27,419
Rochester is so talented and so lively in

243
00:17:27,420 --> 00:17:31,741
society, that I believe he is a general favourite.

244
00:17:32,470 --> 00:17:37,459
The ladies are very fond of him, though you would not think his appearance

245
00:17:37,460 --> 00:17:41,720
calculated to recommend him particularly in their eyes.

246
00:17:43,104 --> 00:17:47,639
But I suppose his requirements and abilities, perhaps his wealth and good

247
00:17:47,640 --> 00:17:51,180
blood, make amends for any little fault of look.

248
00:17:53,020 --> 00:17:54,479
Are there ladies at the knees?

249
00:17:55,959 --> 00:18:02,759
There are Mrs. Eston and her three daughters, very elegant young ladies, indeed.

250
00:18:03,020 --> 00:18:07,439
And there are the honourable blanche and Mary Ingram, most beautiful women,

251
00:18:07,580 --> 00:18:08,580
I suppose.

252
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:12,080
Indeed, I have seen blanche six or seven

253
00:18:12,080 --> 00:18:15,960
years since, when she was a girl of eighteen.

254
00:18:16,540 --> 00:18:20,119
She came here to a Christmas ball and party Mr. Rochester gave.

255
00:18:21,380 --> 00:18:26,159
You should have seen the dining room that day, how richly it was decorated,

256
00:18:26,959 --> 00:18:28,740
how brilliantly lit up.

257
00:18:30,240 --> 00:18:35,439
I should think there were fifty ladies and gentlemen present, all of the first county

258
00:18:35,440 --> 00:18:39,759
families, and Mrs. Ingram was considered the bell of the evening.

259
00:18:41,619 --> 00:18:42,619
You saw her?

260
00:18:43,159 --> 00:18:45,840
You say Mrs. Fairfax, what was she like?

261
00:18:47,490 --> 00:18:49,240
Yes, I saw her.

262
00:18:50,200 --> 00:18:55,060
The dining room doors were thrown open, and, as it was Christmas time,

263
00:18:55,799 --> 00:18:58,242
the servants were allowed to assemble in the

264
00:18:58,243 --> 00:19:01,561
hall to hear some of the ladies sing and play.

265
00:19:02,369 --> 00:19:05,359
Mr. Rochester would have me to come in, and I

266
00:19:05,360 --> 00:19:08,420
sat down in a quiet corner and watched them.

267
00:19:08,709 --> 00:19:10,680
I never saw a more splendid scene.

268
00:19:11,500 --> 00:19:14,419
The ladies were magnificently dressed, most of them.

269
00:19:15,220 --> 00:19:17,633
At least most of the younger ones looked

270
00:19:17,634 --> 00:19:21,260
handsome, but Mrs. Ingram was certainly the queen.

271
00:19:22,250 --> 00:19:23,250
And what was she like?

272
00:19:24,740 --> 00:19:31,220
Tall, fine bust, sloping shoulders, long, graceful neck, olive complexion dark

273
00:19:31,221 --> 00:19:37,439
and clear, noble features, eyes rather like Mr. Rochester's, large and black,

274
00:19:38,060 --> 00:19:39,380
and as brilliant as her jewels.

275
00:19:40,279 --> 00:19:46,721
And then, she had such a fine head of hair, raven black and so becomingly arranged.

276
00:19:47,159 --> 00:19:50,022
A crown of thick plates behind, and in front

277
00:19:50,023 --> 00:19:53,419
the longest, the glossiest curls I ever saw.

278
00:19:54,610 --> 00:19:56,880
She was dressed in pure white.

279
00:19:57,909 --> 00:20:02,720
An amber-colored scarf was passed over her shoulder and across her breast,

280
00:20:03,520 --> 00:20:08,479
tied at the side, and descending in long, fringed ends below her knee.

281
00:20:09,549 --> 00:20:12,459
She wore an amber-colored flower too, in her hair.

282
00:20:13,119 --> 00:20:15,939
It contrasted well with the jetty mass of her curls.

283
00:20:17,569 --> 00:20:19,380
She was greatly admired, of course.

284
00:20:20,279 --> 00:20:21,279
Yes, indeed.

285
00:20:22,110 --> 00:20:24,979
And not only for her beauty, but for her accomplishments.

286
00:20:25,959 --> 00:20:27,979
She was one of the ladies who sang.

287
00:20:28,540 --> 00:20:30,619
A gentleman accompanied her on the piano.

288
00:20:31,419 --> 00:20:34,220
She and Mr. Rochester sang a duet.

289
00:20:35,790 --> 00:20:38,979
Mr. Rochester, I was not aware he could sing.

290
00:20:40,349 --> 00:20:45,099
Oh, he has a fine bass voice and an excellent taste for music.

291
00:20:46,095 --> 00:20:48,959
And Miss Ingram, what sort of a voice had she?

292
00:20:50,009 --> 00:20:51,599
A very rich and powerful one.

293
00:20:52,360 --> 00:20:53,540
She sang delightfully.

294
00:20:54,209 --> 00:20:57,540
It was a treat to listen to her, and she played afterwards.

295
00:20:58,759 --> 00:21:01,939
I am no judge of music, but Mr. Rochester is.

296
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:06,400
And I heard him say her execution was remarkably good.

297
00:21:07,724 --> 00:21:11,220
And this beautiful and accomplished lady, she is not yet married.

298
00:21:12,380 --> 00:21:13,380
It appears not.

299
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:17,880
I fancy neither she nor her sister have very large fortunes.

300
00:21:18,599 --> 00:21:21,221
Old Lord Ingram's estates were chiefly entailed,

301
00:21:21,222 --> 00:21:24,020
and the elder son came in for everything almost.

302
00:21:26,400 --> 00:21:30,580
But I wonder no wealthy nobleman or gentleman has taken a fancy to her.

303
00:21:31,180 --> 00:21:32,520
Mr. Rochester, for instance.

304
00:21:33,360 --> 00:21:34,659
He is rich, is he not?

305
00:21:35,819 --> 00:21:36,819
Oh, yes.

306
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:40,119
But you see there is a considerable difference in age.

307
00:21:40,900 --> 00:21:42,380
Mr. Rochester is nearly 40.

308
00:21:42,979 --> 00:21:44,060
She is but 25.

309
00:21:45,700 --> 00:21:46,700
What of that?

310
00:21:46,880 --> 00:21:48,720
More unequal matches are made every day.

311
00:21:49,860 --> 00:21:50,860
True.

312
00:21:51,159 --> 00:21:55,939
Yet I should scarcely fancy Mr. Rochester would entertain an idea of the sort.

313
00:21:56,965 --> 00:21:57,965
But you eat nothing.

314
00:21:58,700 --> 00:22:01,180
You have scarcely tasted since you began tea.

315
00:22:02,639 --> 00:22:05,520
No, I am too thirsty to eat.

316
00:22:06,060 --> 00:22:07,380
Will you let me have another cup?

317
00:22:09,090 --> 00:22:12,979
I was about again to revert to the probability of a union between Mr.

318
00:22:13,180 --> 00:22:15,860
Rochester and the beautiful blanche.

319
00:22:16,889 --> 00:22:21,299
But a del came in and the conversation was turned into another channel.

320
00:22:22,625 --> 00:22:28,020
When once more alone, I reviewed the information I had got, looked into my

321
00:22:28,021 --> 00:22:33,919
heart, examined its thoughts and feelings, and endeavored to bring back with a strict

322
00:22:33,920 --> 00:22:39,439
hand such as had been straining through imaginations boundless and trackless waste

323
00:22:40,064 --> 00:22:42,479
into the safe fold of common sense.

324
00:22:43,720 --> 00:22:48,819
Arrained at my own bar, memory having given her evidence of the hopes,

325
00:22:49,479 --> 00:22:53,119
wishes, sentiments I had been cherishing since last night.

326
00:22:54,270 --> 00:22:58,840
Of the general state of mind, in which I had indulged for nearly a fortnight past,

327
00:22:59,930 --> 00:23:04,720
reason haven't come forward and told in her own quiet way a plain unvarnished

328
00:23:04,721 --> 00:23:10,720
tale, showing how I had rejected the real and rapidly devoured the ideal.

329
00:23:11,909 --> 00:23:17,479
I pronounced judgment to this effect, that a greater fool than Jane Eyre had

330
00:23:17,480 --> 00:23:23,000
never breathed the breath of life, that a more fantastic idiot had never

331
00:23:23,001 --> 00:23:28,439
surfated herself on sweet lies and swallowed poison as if it were nectar.

332
00:23:29,770 --> 00:23:35,659
You, I said, a favourite with Mr. Rochester, you gifted with the power of

333
00:23:35,661 --> 00:23:38,740
pleasing him, you of importance to him in any way?

334
00:23:39,669 --> 00:23:45,319
Go, your folly sickened me, and you have derived pleasure from occasional tokens of

335
00:23:45,320 --> 00:23:49,323
preference, equivocal tokens shown by a gentleman of

336
00:23:49,324 --> 00:23:53,500
family and a man of the world, to a dependent and a novice.

337
00:23:54,159 --> 00:23:55,159
How dared you?

338
00:23:55,900 --> 00:24:00,560
Poor stupid dupe, could not even self -interest make you wiser.

339
00:24:01,479 --> 00:24:04,840
You repeated to yourself this morning the brief scene of last night.

340
00:24:05,840 --> 00:24:07,319
Cover your face and be ashamed.

341
00:24:08,360 --> 00:24:10,779
He said something in praise of your eyes, did he?

342
00:24:11,630 --> 00:24:17,860
Blind puppy, open their bled lids and look on your own accursed senselessness.

343
00:24:19,299 --> 00:24:24,080
It does good to no woman to be flattered by her superior, who cannot possibly

344
00:24:24,080 --> 00:24:29,840
intend to marry her, and it is madness in all women, to let a secret love kindle

345
00:24:29,841 --> 00:24:34,639
within them, which, if unreturned and unknown, must devour the life that feeds

346
00:24:35,490 --> 00:24:41,742
it, and, if discovered and responded to, must lead, igneus,

347
00:24:41,743 --> 00:24:46,119
fatuous, like into myriwilds once there is no extrication.

348
00:24:47,259 --> 00:24:49,119
Listen then, Jane Eyre, to your sentence.

349
00:24:50,319 --> 00:24:55,099
Tomorrow, place the glass before you, and draw in chalk your own picture,

350
00:24:55,759 --> 00:25:01,900
faithfully, without softening one defect, omit no harsh line, smooth away no

351
00:25:01,901 --> 00:25:05,325
displeasing irregularity, right under it, portrait

352
00:25:05,326 --> 00:25:08,681
of a governess disconnected poor and plain.

353
00:25:09,849 --> 00:25:12,759
Afterwards, take a piece of smooth ivory.

354
00:25:13,750 --> 00:25:15,599
You have one prepared in your drawing box.

355
00:25:16,700 --> 00:25:23,720
Take your palette, mix your freshest, finest, clearest tints, choose your most

356
00:25:23,721 --> 00:25:28,819
delicate camelhair pencils, delineate carefully the loveliest face you can

357
00:25:28,820 --> 00:25:34,720
imagine, paint it in your softer shades and sweetest lines, according to the

358
00:25:34,721 --> 00:25:37,639
description given by Mrs. Fairfax of Blanche Ingram.

359
00:25:38,779 --> 00:25:41,700
Remember the raven ringlets, the oriental eye.

360
00:25:42,750 --> 00:25:49,639
What, you revert to Mr. Rochester as a model, order, no snivel, no sentiment,

361
00:25:50,240 --> 00:25:54,500
no regret, I will endure only sense and resolution.

362
00:25:55,659 --> 00:26:00,159
Recall the august, yet harmonious lineaments, the greekian neck and bust,

363
00:26:00,990 --> 00:26:06,400
let the round and dazzling arm be visible, and the delicate hand, omit neither

364
00:26:06,401 --> 00:26:10,740
diamond ring nor gold bracelet, portray faithfully the attire,

365
00:26:11,200 --> 00:26:16,159
aerial lace and glistening satin, graceful scarf and golden rose,

366
00:26:17,150 --> 00:26:20,639
call its Blanche, an accomplished lady of rank.

367
00:26:22,380 --> 00:26:27,099
Whenever in future you should chance to fancy Mr. Rochester thinks well of you,

368
00:26:27,779 --> 00:26:31,360
take out these two pictures and compare them, say.

369
00:26:33,209 --> 00:26:39,161
Mr. Rochester might probably win that noble lady's love if he chose to strive for it.

370
00:26:40,279 --> 00:26:43,575
Is it likely he would waste a serious thought

371
00:26:43,576 --> 00:26:47,260
on this indigent and insignificant plebeian?

372
00:26:48,259 --> 00:26:51,586
I'll do it, I resolved, and having framed this

373
00:26:51,587 --> 00:26:55,420
determination, I grew calm and fell asleep.

374
00:26:55,860 --> 00:27:01,419
I kept my word, an hour or two sufficed to sketch my own portrait in crayons,

375
00:27:02,180 --> 00:27:05,611
and in less than a fortnight I had completed an

376
00:27:05,612 --> 00:27:08,939
ivory miniature of an imaginary Blanche Ingram.

377
00:27:10,250 --> 00:27:14,759
It looked a lovely face enough, and when compared with the real head in

378
00:27:14,760 --> 00:27:19,520
chalk, the contrast was as great as self -control could desire.

379
00:27:20,810 --> 00:27:23,119
I derived benefit from the task.

380
00:27:23,985 --> 00:27:30,240
It had kept my head and hands employed and had given force and fix itness to the new

381
00:27:30,241 --> 00:27:34,419
impressions I wished to stamp indelibly on my heart.

382
00:27:35,279 --> 00:27:39,549
Air long, I had reason to congratulate myself on the course of wholesome

383
00:27:39,550 --> 00:27:44,069
discipline to which I had thus forced my feelings to submit.

384
00:27:46,279 --> 00:27:51,950
Thanks to it, I was able to meet subsequent occurrences with a decent calm,

385
00:27:53,040 --> 00:27:56,527
which had they found me unprepared, I should probably

386
00:27:56,528 --> 00:27:59,950
have been unequal to maintain, even externally.
